# DS-0026 (HEALTHCHECK): not applicable to tests/e2e/Containerfile. That image
# is a one-shot test runner — compose invokes `command: ["venom", "run", ...]`
# and the container exits when the suite finishes (see tests/e2e/compose.yaml).
# A Docker HEALTHCHECK only has meaning for long-running services; adding one to
# a one-shot runner would be misleading no-op config, so the finding is ignored
# rather than silenced with a meaningless probe.
#
# This is a .trivyignore entry rather than an inline `#trivy:ignore:` comment
# because DS-0026 is a line-less, whole-image check (missing instruction): its
# finding carries no source line for an inline directive to attach to, so inline
# ignores do not suppress it in trivy 0.71.x.
DS-0026
